{"tool": "finish", "summary": "Added the per-user feed limit `max_feeds` (0 = unlimited). The build and existing unit and integration tests pass; the new behaviour itself has no tests of its own yet.\n\n- **Schema and model:** a new migration adds `users.max_feeds` (int, not null, default 0). The field is on the user object and the modification request, in both the server model and the Go client.\n- **Admin-only update:** `PUT /v1/users/{userID}` returns 400 if a non-admin sends `max_feeds` at all, even with the current value, and 400 for a negative value.\n- **Enforcement:** the check lives in `Storage.CreateFeed`, the only place feeds are inserted, so it covers the API, the UI, the Google Reader API and OPML import. It locks the user row, counts feeds and inserts in one transaction, so concurrent requests cannot push a user past the limit.\n- **`POST /v1/feeds`:** returns 400 and creates nothing once the user is at the limit.\n- **`POST /v1/import`:** imports feeds until the limit is reached, then stops and returns 400. Feeds imported before that point are kept, so an over-sized import is partial rather than rejected up front.\n\nTwo things you might not expect:\n- The limit error message is a plain English string, not a translated locale key.\n- `UpdateUser` writes `max_feeds` in a separate statement after the main update rather than in the same query.", "t": 1794463776.428}
{"tool": "_result", "name": "finish", "chars": 55, "t": 1794463776.428}
